Instead of page protecting the lock the data structure is page protected with two separate
pointers for reading and writing. Writers PROT_NONE the reader page before making changes.

This also has the 2 known problems with seqlocks:
<a> can only snapshot .. cant produce external side effects while holding reader lock

<b> can't chase pointers

---------------- Details ------------------------

Its no different than the other one except that the data ptr is provided by this API.

There are two pointers rptr, wptr the rptr is posix_memalign allocated with mprotect.
Write locks mremap wptr to rptr and later gives it back with sufficient fences.

